things that I'm excited

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.380
about this event because I feel like

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.590
it'll probably be celebrity driven.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:21.220
I think they'll probably have a lot

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.530
of really cool people out to talk

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:23.870
about the shows that they're working on.

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:26.010
One of the things that
I feel like I've been

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:29.200
hitting recently is subscription fatigue.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.039
I don't really have cable anymore,

00:01:31.039 --> 00:01:33.570
but the amount that I
was spending on cable,

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.690
I think I'm probably spending double that

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.120
on everything that I'm subscribed to,

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:42.700
from Netflix to Hulu to Amazon to Spotify

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:45.300
to Apple Music to various fitness apps

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.360
to Peloton to just so many things.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.090
I was going through some
of the apps that I use

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.060
and it was like, what?

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:51.893
I didn't even realize some

00:01:51.893 --> 00:01:54.340
of these things were
still charging like $1.99.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.990
So if you guys do have
subscriptions to apps,

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:59.520
I would recommend going in
at least every few months

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.520
and just checking to make sure
that you're not being charged

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.490
for something that you're not using.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.530
There was even a yoga
app that I had signed up

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.940
for just to test it but
it wouldn't let me login

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.580
without actually subscribing,

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:09.980
and I did this like two months ago.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.420
I didn't even take a single yoga class

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:12.980
and now I'm canceling my subscription.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.450
So it definitely is good to go in

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:16.510
and just kind of assess
what are the things that

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:18.050
you actually use and what do you need.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:19.420
But of course this is Apple so

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.720
